 "summary": "The regular-expression pattern language of ECMA-262 (JavaScript), specified with a formal grammar and a continuation-passing matcher semantics; Perl-derived backtracking syntax extended over time with sticky/unicode flags (ES2015), named groups, lookbehind and dotAll (ES2018), match indices, the v flag with set notation (ES2024) and inline modifiers.",
 "status": "active",
 "defined_by": [
  "international-standard"
 ],
 "standards": [
  "ECMA-262 §22.2 RegExp (Regular Expression) Objects",
  "ISO/IEC 16262"
 ],
 "homepage": "https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-regexp-regular-expression-objects",
 "influenced_by": [
  "pcre"
 ],
 "related": [
  {
   "id": "javascript",
   "relation": "embeds"
  },
  {
   "id": "pcre",
   "relation": "family"
  }
 ],
 "level_notes": {
  "1": "ECMA-262 clause 22.2 gives the Pattern grammar and its semantics as matcher/continuation abstract operations; Annex B.1.2 adds legacy web-compatibility syntax. Deep links target the living draft at tc39.es; new syntax arrives through TC39 proposals.",
  "0": "V8's Irregexp (backtracking compiler/interpreter plus an experimental linear-time engine, also used by SpiderMonkey) and QuickJS's libregexp; test262 holds conformance tests."
 },
